Hills Home offers, a cursor marketplace backdoor, and a Ukraine starlink throttle come next.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.820
Then the counterpoint and the engineering deep dive. The Federal Communications Commission voted

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.360
Thursday to advance a proposal raising eligible satellite direct-to-phone bands from 5-13.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:35.540
14, according to KeepTrack, though no bands have been assigned yet. AT&amp;T, Verizon, and

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:41.300
T-Mobile, through the wireless trade group CTIA, asked the commission to drop the 2.5

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:49.020
GHz and 3.45 GHz bands, which account for 290 MHz of the total. T-Mobile argued satellite

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:55.320
interference could eliminate up to 96% of a cell site's uplink coverage area. SpaceX asked

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:02.980
the FCC to add the 902-928 megahertz band. A companion item proposes auctioning 25 megahertz

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:13.820
in the 1,675-1,695 megahertz and 2020-2,025 megahertz bands, usable for terrestrial service,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.760
direct to device service, or both, with commons due 60 days after the notice appears in the Federal

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:27.900
Register. The Starlink constellation stands at 13,069 satellites launched, 11,199 in orbit,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:34.940
and 11,176 working, while the conjunction catalogs Socrates lists seven upcoming Starlink

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:40.760
events among its top probability cases, non-rated high-risk, two of them carrying physically

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.680
implausible numbers that should be treated as stale, and two satellites with active reentry

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.212
predictions as they decay toward planned disposal. Colonial Hills, a neighborhood in South

00:01:51.212 --> 00:01:56.532
Haven, has been getting buyout approaches covering as many as 418 homes, according to

00:01:56.532 --> 00:02:01.392
Big Go. The community sits roughly half a mile from the power plant that supplies electricity

00:02:01.392 --> 00:02:06.392
to the company's data centers in the area. The buyout carries a condition that sellers must

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:11.272
agree not to join the class action litigation over noise from the gas turbines that run the

00:02:11.272 --> 00:02:18.172
facilities GPUs. The subsidiary operating the Colossus 2 site, MZX, sent an open letter

00:02:18.172 --> 00:02:21.492
to residents saying it requires property for its business purposes.

00:02:22.132 --> 00:02:26.512
South Haven mayor Darren Muscle White said the acquired homes would house SpaceX and

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:32.152
XAI staff as the company's expand, describing the program as a goodwill gesture from a good

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:37.172
corporate citizen for those who perceive the industrial development near them as negative, and he

00:02:37.172 --> 00:02:40.852
He said the purchases are not meant to turn colonial hills into a company town.

00:02:41.472 --> 00:02:45.232
Musk has been staying in the neighborhood in an air-stream trailer four nights a week,

00:02:45.712 --> 00:02:49.652
personally overseeing the build-out of capacity needed to power the GROC chatbot.

00:02:50.662 --> 00:02:55.722
Cursor disclosed a security incident involving a maliciously modified version of the anthropic

00:02:55.722 --> 00:02:58.422
clawed code extension in its VS code marketplace.

00:02:58.982 --> 00:03:02.722
Business Standard reports the package was not developed by anthropic.

00:03:02.722 --> 00:03:09.042
Rancode attempting to install a persistent secure shell, or SSH, backdoor, and affected

00:03:09.042 --> 00:03:10.522
at most 5,000 users.

00:03:11.022 --> 00:03:15.142
The malicious package was available for roughly 11 hours on October 29.

00:03:15.682 --> 00:03:21.642
It collected host and user information, including host name, user name, operating system, and

00:03:21.642 --> 00:03:23.282
the machine's public IP address.

00:03:23.742 --> 00:03:27.762
Tried to add an attacker-controlled SSH key and opened a reverse tunnel.

00:03:27.762 --> 00:03:32.542
A step the company said would fail unless Cursor was started with Administrator privileges,

00:03:33.062 --> 00:03:35.882
and still installed persistence and sent host details.

00:03:36.522 --> 00:03:41.722
For persistence, the payload installs a Mac login agent called a launch agent, or on

00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:46.682
Windows a scheduled task that attempts to run at the highest system privilege, with background

00:03:46.682 --> 00:03:49.702
scripts retrying the tunnel roughly every 60 seconds.

00:03:50.302 --> 00:03:55.642
Cursor removed the malicious version, shut down the entire marketplace as a precaution, confirmed

00:03:55.642 --> 00:04:00.662
no other extensions were tampered with, rotated its keys, rebuilt the marketplace,

00:04:01.042 --> 00:04:05.882
and worked with the cloud provider to take the attacker's server offline, leaving the reverse shell

00:04:05.882 --> 00:04:11.737
non-functional. Elon Musk acknowledged over the weekend that SpaceX had throttled Starlink in

00:04:11.737 --> 00:04:18.017
Ukraine, and accused Ukraine of violating Starlink's terms of service, a charge Ukrainian officials rejected.

00:04:18.697 --> 00:04:23.437
Ars Technica reports Musk wrote that the loophole was closed last week and that star shield,

00:04:23.437 --> 00:04:26.497
a different system is controlled by the U.S. government.

00:04:27.157 --> 00:04:31.737
Ukrainian officials reported that military drones lost satellite connectivity when traveling

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:37.277
