00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.380
Closing a phone to satellite link from an engineering standpoint is a fight

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:57.320
against distance and millawatts, not a shortage of towers. A handheld phone puts

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.400
out only a few hundred millawatts of radio energy, while a terrestrial cell

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:06.080
site sits a few hundred meters away and can run a few tens of watts. Free space

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:11.320
This path loss at a couple of gigahertz across hundreds of kilometers is, on a back-of-envelope

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.860
figure, on the order of 150 decibels, so received power shrinks by a factor of about

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:17.860
10 to the 15.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:24.780
Thermal noise in a one-hertz bandwidth sits near minus 174 decibels milliwatts, a textbook

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:29.340
floor, so every extra decibel of path loss eats into the bits you can push.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:34.680
Shannon's formula says that in the moderate signal to noise regime, more hertz at the same

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:38.500
ratio raises the data rate without asking the handset to shout louder.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:44.180
In the extremely power-limited limit, capacity approaches a ceiling set by received power

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.220
over noise density.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:51.140
So extra spectrum helps more as cleaner channels and as reuse of the same hertz in non-overlapping

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.680
spot beams, meaning narrow radio footprints on the ground.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:08:00.440
Each new megahertz can be painted onto a different patch of earth at the same time, so system

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:05.160
Some capacity scales with both bandwidth and the number of simultaneous beams the satellites

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.940
phased array antennas can form.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:12.580
Because the satellites already carry inter-satellite laser links, a direct-to-cell user's bits

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:17.120
can leave the serving beam and ride the mesh to a ground station instead of fighting for a

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.900
return path in the same frequency.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:24.680
The magic wand number is hertz reused across beams rather than extra millawatts in your pocket,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:30.960
And the idiot index is that 15 orders of magnitude gap that coding, antenna gain, and frequency

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.160
reuse have to close.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.280
Wider contiguous channels let the modem extract more bits per jewel at the handset.

